//@version=6
// =============================================================================
// BASIC BREAKS  —  numbered off ACCURATE HH / HL / LH / LL structure
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT CHANGED, AND WHY
//
//   The old build read ta.pivothigh and ta.pivotlow as two INDEPENDENT series.
//   They do not alternate. Inside one leg you can get three pivot highs in a row
//   with no pivot low between them, and all three went on the stack as separate
//   levels. Three levels where structure has ONE. That is what made a genuine
//   2nd print as a 3rd, and what put a level in a place nothing turned.
//
//   This build makes the structure alternate, the way it is read by hand:
//
//     · a swing HIGH must be followed by a swing LOW before another high counts
//     · while the leg is still running, the more extreme point REPLACES the one
//       standing — a higher high inside an up leg is the same swing, moved
//     · so every swing is one turning point, and they run high · low · high · low
//
//   Each swing is then classified against the previous swing ON ITS OWN SIDE:
//
//     HH  swing high ABOVE the last swing high        LH  below it
//     HL  swing low  ABOVE the last swing low         LL  below it
//
//   A decline leaves LH · LL · LH · LL behind it. A rally leaves HH · HL.
//
// THE BREAKS
//   Unchanged in spirit — the move takes the structure back NEWEST FIRST:
//
//       the LAST swing high made     →  1st Break        (buy setups)
//       the one before it            →  2nd Break
//       the one before that          →  3rd Break        … and so on.
//
//   Lows are the mirror, for sell setups. A level leaves for one reason only:
//   price broke it. The count restarts at 1st the moment a break takes a swing
//   NEWER than the last one numbered — that is the move eating structure it
//   built itself, which is a different leg.
//
//   Restricting the buy side to LH only (and the sell side to HL only) is
//   optional and OFF by default: an HH is still a level price has to take, and
//   it is usually the swing that topped the decline — the last number in the
//   sequence, not something to drop.
//
// DEAD HOURS  (new — 21:00 → 01:30 by default, and ON)
//   Nothing is treated as a setup between 21:00 and 01:30. Inside that window a
//   sequence cannot start, no break is drawn, no entry fires, no alert fires and
//   nothing reaches the results.
//
//   What it does NOT do — and this is the part that matters: structure keeps
//   being read and levels keep being CONSUMED. A break that happened, happened.
//   Skipping the bookkeeping would leave dead levels standing and the numbering
//   after the window would be wrong. So the window silences the output; it never
//   edits the structure the numbering is built from.
//
//   Times are read in Africa/Johannesburg (SAST) by default, so 21:00 means the
//   21:00 you see on your own clock. Change the zone, the window, the days, or
//   turn the whole thing off — nothing else in the script changes.
//
// Non-repainting: swings are CONFIRMED pivots (placed `length` bars back) and a
// break is judged once at bar close. A wick through that closes back inside is
// a fake-out and breaks nothing.
//
// The HH / HL / LH / LL labels and the zigzag are OFF. Nothing is drawn on the
// chart that was not asked for; turn them on in "Structure labels" to check the
// reading, turn them off again and the numbering is untouched.
// =============================================================================
indicator("Basic Breaks", "BREAKS", overlay = true, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_boxes_count = 100)

// ===================== STRUCTURE =============================================
gSt = "Structure"
pvLen = input.int(1, "Swing length  —  1 = EVERY turning point, no matter how small", minval = 1, group = gSt, tooltip = "Bars that must be clear either side of a turning point.\n\n1 (default) — every turning point counts, however small. A two-bar bounce inside a decline is a swing.\n\nAnything higher THROWS SMALL TURNING POINTS AWAY. At 5, a bounce needs five bars clear on each side to exist at all, so small ones are never swings and never get numbered.")
lhOnly = input.bool(false, "Buys: only break LOWER highs  ·  Sells: only HIGHER lows", group = gSt, tooltip = "OFF by default.\n\nOff — every swing high is a level for the buy side, whether it is an LH or the HH that topped the decline. The HH is normally the LAST number in the sequence, so dropping it loses the far end of the leg.\n\nOn — only swings classified LH are levels for buys, only HL for sells. Strict structure reading. Turn it on to see the difference; it is the whole point of this build being switchable.")
minLv = input.int(2, "A side counts once it has N levels", minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = gSt, tooltip = "A single stray swing is not a sequence. Requiring 2 means at least two levels must exist before breaks are numbered. Set to 1 to number everything.")
sellOn = input.bool(true, "Track LOWS  (broken downward → sell setups)", group = gSt)
buyOn = input.bool(true, "Track HIGHS  (broken upward → buy setups)", group = gSt)
swMax = input.int(60, "Track at most N swings", minval = 4, maxval = 400, group = gSt, tooltip = "Bounds the structure. When it is full the OLDEST swing is dropped — and in a decline the oldest is the highest, the one furthest from price. If a deep move stops being numbered part-way, raise this.")

// ===================== BREAK CONFIRMATION ====================================
gCf = "Break confirmation"
confMode = input.string("Close beyond", "What breaks a level", options = ["Wick beyond", "Close beyond", "Full body beyond"], group = gCf, tooltip = "Close beyond (default) — the candle must FINISH past the level. A wick through that closes back inside is a fake-out and breaks nothing.\nFull body beyond — open AND close both clear. Stricter.\nWick beyond — any touch counts, fake-outs included.")
waitClose = input.bool(true, "Only judge closed bars", group = gCf, tooltip = "On (default): a break is decided at the close of the candle and never redrawn. This is what makes the entry signal fire in real time on that close.")

// ===================== DEAD HOURS ============================================
// The window kills OUTPUT, not bookkeeping. Levels are still consumed inside it,
// because a break that happened cannot be un-happened without corrupting every
// number that comes after it. See the header.
gTh = "Dead hours  (no setups in this window)"
thOn = input.bool(true, "Kill every setup inside a time window", group = gTh, tooltip = "ON by default, set to 21:00 → 01:30.\n\nInside the window: no sequence can start, nothing is drawn, no entry fires, no alert fires, nothing reaches the results.\n\nOutside it: unchanged.\n\nStructure and level-consumption keep running either way — that is deliberate, and turning this off restores the old behaviour exactly.")
thWin = input.session("2100-0130", "The window", group = gTh, tooltip = "HHMM-HHMM. 2100-0130 = 9pm to half past one the following morning; a window that crosses midnight is handled properly.\n\nThe start is inclusive and the end is exclusive: a bar at 01:30 is already outside and can trade.")
thTz = input.string("Africa/Johannesburg", "Read the window in this timezone", options = ["Africa/Johannesburg", "America/New_York", "Europe/London", "Asia/Tokyo", "UTC", "Exchange"], group = gTh, tooltip = "Africa/Johannesburg = SAST (UTC+2), so you type the hours exactly as you see them on your own clock. Daylight saving in the chosen zone is handled by TradingView, per date — a New York window does not drift in March and November.\n\nExchange = the chart's own timezone.")
thDays = input.string("1234567", "Days the window applies to", group = gTh, tooltip = "1=Sunday … 7=Saturday. Leave as 1234567 for every day. A window across midnight is stamped by the day it OPENS.")
thWhat = input.string("Everything in the window", "What the window kills", options = ["Everything in the window", "Only the entry"], group = gTh, tooltip = "Everything (default) — a sequence whose 1st Break lands inside the window is dead for its whole life, and nothing at all is drawn or fired while the window is open. This is the literal reading: no setups between those hours.\n\nOnly the entry — breaks still draw, still number and still fire the break alert inside the window, but no entry is taken and nothing reaches the results. Use this one if you want to SEE what the dead hours are doing without trading them.")
thShade = input.bool(false, "Shade the dead hours on the chart", group = gTh, tooltip = "Off by default. Turn it on once to confirm with your own eyes that the shading covers exactly the candles you meant, then turn it off.")
thShadeC = input.color(color.new(#F23645, 92), "Shade", group = gTh)

// ===================== IS THIS ACTUALLY A SETUP? =============================
// Structure is still read at every turning point, however small — that has not
// changed and it is not going to. What HAS changed is that not every sequence
// is a trade. A two-bar wiggle taken back by another two-bar wiggle is a break;
// it is not a setup, and 786 of them at 37.8% is what that costs.
//
// A sequence qualifies at its 1st Break, on the size of the leg it is taking
// back — the distance from that level down to the low the move came off (up to
// the high, for sells). Everything below the bar is still counted in structure,
// it just does not get drawn, does not get an entry, and does not go into the
// results.
gQ = "Is this actually a setup?"
qOn = input.bool(true, "Only trade a sequence if the leg is worth trading", group = gQ, tooltip = "ON by default. Turn it off to go back to numbering and trading every sequence, which is what produced hundreds of trades at a losing profit factor.")
minLegAtr = input.float(2.5, "…the leg must be at least (× ATR)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 20.0, step = 0.1, group = gQ, tooltip = "THIS IS THE DIAL. Measured at the 1st Break: the distance from the level being broken down to the low the move came off, in ATRs.\n\nRaise it for fewer, bigger, cleaner setups. Lower it for more. Watch the dashboard — trades, win %, profit factor — and stop where the profit factor is best, not where the trade count is highest.")
qTrend = input.bool(false, "…and structure must already have turned", group = gQ, tooltip = "OFF by default. On, a buy sequence only counts once the last swing low is an HL (the decline has stopped making lower lows) and a sell sequence once the last swing high is an LH.\n\nIt cuts the count hard and takes the entry later. Try it second, after the leg size is set.")
drawSkipped = input.bool(false, "Draw the sequences that did not qualify", group = gQ, tooltip = "OFF by default — this is what takes the mess off the chart. The skipped sequences are still counted in the structure, they are just not drawn.\n\nIt does not override the dead hours: a sequence killed by the clock stays off the chart.")

// ===================== STRUCTURE LABELS ======================================
gZz = "Structure labels  (HH / HL / LH / LL)"
zzLbl = input.bool(false, "Label every swing HH / HL / LH / LL", group = gZz, tooltip = "OFF by default. Turn it on to read the structure the numbering is built from, then turn it off again — it changes nothing except what is drawn.")
zzLine = input.bool(false, "Join the swings with a zigzag", group = gZz)
zzN = input.int(20, "…only the last N swings", minval = 2, maxval = 200, group = gZz)
zzUpC = input.color(color.new(#089981, 0), "HH / HL", inline = "zc", group = gZz)
zzDnC = input.color(color.new(#F23645, 0), "LH / LL", inline = "zc", group = gZz)
zzLnC = input.color(color.new(#787B86, 45), "Zigzag", inline = "zc", group = gZz)

// ===================== THE LIVE LEVELS =======================================
gLs = "The levels still standing"
stackShow = input.bool(false, "Show the levels nothing has broken yet", group = gLs, tooltip = "OFF by default. A dotted line for every swing still unbroken, numbered outward from price — 1 is the next one that breaks, and it is the one that will be labelled 1st Break.\n\nIt is a preview of the numbering, not part of it: turning it off changes nothing about the break marks or the dashboard.")
stackHLC = input.color(color.new(#089981, 40), "Lows", inline = "sc", group = gLs)
stackLHC = input.color(color.new(#F23645, 40), "Highs", inline = "sc", group = gLs)
stackTag = input.bool(false, "Number them from the top", group = gLs)

// ===================== VISUALS ===============================================
gVs = "Visuals"
hidePast = input.bool(true, "Only draw the first N breaks", group = gVs, tooltip = "ON by default: only the 1st, 2nd and 3rd are drawn.\n\nThe count always keeps running underneath — a 4th, 5th or 6th break still happens, still fires the alert and still shows in the dashboard. This only stops them being DRAWN.\n\nTurn it off to put every break in the sequence on the chart.")
hidePastN = input.int(3, "…how many", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = gVs)
histBars = input.int(300, "Only show breaks from the last N bars  (0 = all history)", minval = 0, maxval = 5000, group = gVs, tooltip = "THIS is the control for clutter. Everything inside the window is numbered and drawn; everything older is cleared off the chart.")
cN1 = input.color(color.new(#5B9CF6, 0), "1st", inline = "cn", group = gVs)
cN2 = input.color(color.new(#2962FF, 0), "2nd", inline = "cn", group = gVs)
cN3 = input.color(color.new(#089981, 0), "3rd", inline = "cn", group = gVs)
cNx = input.color(color.new(#787B86, 0), "4th+", inline = "cn", group = gVs)
lineOn = input.bool(true, "Draw the broken level as a line", group = gVs)
lineW = input.int(1, "Line width", minval = 1, maxval = 4, group = gVs)
lineStyleIn = input.string("Solid", "Line style", options = ["Solid", "Dashed", "Dotted"], group = gVs)
lblOn = input.bool(true, "Label the break", group = gVs)
lblFmt = input.string("1st Break", "Label text", options = ["1st Break", "1st", "1st Break + price", "1st Break + kind", "1"], group = gVs, tooltip = "\"1st Break + kind\" puts the structure label on it — \"2nd Break LH\" — so you can see exactly which swing took that number.")
lblPos = input.string("Centre", "Label sits", options = ["Left", "Centre", "Right"], group = gVs)
lblOff = input.float(0.25, "Label offset (× ATR)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 3.0, step = 0.05, group = gVs)
lblSzIn = input.string("Small", "Label size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large"], group = gVs)

// ===================== ENTRY =================================================
gEn = "Entry"
entOn = input.bool(false, "Mark an entry on the Nth break", group = gEn, tooltip = "A marker on the candle you enter plus an \"E: Long\" / \"E: Short\" label. Fires the moment the candle that makes the Nth break CLOSES.\n\nAn entry inside the dead hours never fires, whichever setting the dead-hours group is on.")
entAt = input.int(2, "…on which break", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = gEn)
entShift = input.int(1, "Marker sits N candles after the break candle", minval = 0, maxval = 10, group = gEn)
entTxtBuy = input.string("E: Long", "Buy label", inline = "et", group = gEn)
entTxtSell = input.string("E: Short", "Sell label", inline = "et", group = gEn)
entShape = input.string("Triangle", "Marker", options = ["Triangle", "Circle", "Arrow", "Diamond"], group = gEn)
entSzIn = input.string("Normal", "Marker size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large", "Huge"], group = gEn)
entTxtSz = input.string("Normal", "Label text size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large", "Huge"], group = gEn)
entBuyC = input.color(#00BF71, "Buy", inline = "ec", group = gEn)
entSellC = input.color(#FF4F87, "Sell", inline = "ec", group = gEn)
entPad = input.float(0.35, "Marker gap from the candle (× ATR)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 3.0, step = 0.05, group = gEn)

// ===================== RESULTS ===============================================
// Not a Strategy. Indicator-side numbers: no spread, no slippage, no commission,
// no partial fills, one position at a time. They tell you how the SIGNAL behaved
// on this timeframe's bars, nothing more.
gRs = "Results  (dashboard stats)"
resOn = input.bool(true, "Track wins / losses on this timeframe", group = gRs, tooltip = "Follows the same signal the entry arrows use — the Nth break — whether or not the arrows are switched on. Switching timeframe recalculates from that timeframe's bars.\n\nA trade already open when the dead hours start is left alone to hit its stop or its target. The window stops setups being TAKEN; it does not liquidate one that was.")
stopMode = input.string("Structure (the swing behind it)", "Stop", options = ["Structure (the swing behind it)", "Fixed × ATR"], group = gRs, tooltip = "Structure: the newest unbroken swing behind the entry — the low the move came off for a long, the high for a short. That is where the idea is wrong.\nFixed: a flat multiple of ATR.")
stopAtr = input.float(1.0, "…ATR multiple (also the fallback)", minval = 0.1, maxval = 10.0, step = 0.1, group = gRs)
tgtMode = input.string("Nearest opposite level", "Target", options = ["Nearest opposite level", "Opposite extreme (draw on liquidity)", "R multiple"], group = gRs, tooltip = "NEAREST (default) — the first unbroken swing the other side of entry. It is the level price actually has to get through next, and it is reachable.\n\nOpposite extreme — the FURTHEST unbroken swing, the full draw on liquidity. It is the right idea on a big leg and the wrong one on a small one: aiming at it on every sequence is most of why the win rate was 37.8%. A target three times further away than the stop cannot win half the time.\n\nR multiple — a flat multiple of the risk.\n\nAll three fall back to the R multiple when there is nothing standing the other side.")
tgtR = input.float(2.0, "…R multiple (also the fallback)", minval = 0.1, maxval = 20.0, step = 0.1, group = gRs)

// ===================== DASHBOARD =============================================
gDb = "Dashboard"
dbOn = input.bool(true, "Show dashboard", group = gDb)
dbPos = input.string("Top right", "Position", options = ["Top right", "Top left", "Bottom right", "Bottom left", "Middle right"], group = gDb)
dbSzIn = input.string("Tiny", "Text size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal"], group = gDb)

// ===================== HELPERS ===============================================
f_size(string s) =>
    s == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : s == "Small" ? size.small : s == "Normal" ? size.normal : s == "Huge" ? size.huge : size.large

f_lstyle(string s) =>
    s == "Dashed" ? line.style_dashed : s == "Dotted" ? line.style_dotted : line.style_solid

f_tpos(string s) =>
    switch s
        "Top left" => position.top_left
        "Bottom right" => position.bottom_right
        "Bottom left" => position.bottom_left
        "Middle right" => position.middle_right
        => position.top_right

f_ord(int n) =>
    int r100 = n % 100
    int r10 = n % 10
    string sfx = r100 >= 11 and r100 <= 13 ? "th" : r10 == 1 ? "st" : r10 == 2 ? "nd" : r10 == 3 ? "rd" : "th"
    str.tostring(n) + sfx

// 1 HH · 2 HL · 3 LH · 4 LL · 0 the first swing on its side, nothing to compare
f_kind(int k) =>
    k == 1 ? "HH" : k == 2 ? "HL" : k == 3 ? "LH" : k == 4 ? "LL" : "—"

f_txt(int n, float px, int k) =>
    switch lblFmt
        "1st Break" => f_ord(n) + " Break"
        "1st" => f_ord(n)
        "1st Break + price" => f_ord(n) + " Break " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(px))
        "1st Break + kind" => f_ord(n) + " Break " + f_kind(k)
        => str.tostring(n)

f_eshape(string sh, bool up) =>
    sh == "Circle" ? label.style_circle : sh == "Diamond" ? label.style_diamond : sh == "Arrow" ? (up ? label.style_arrowup : label.style_arrowdown) : (up ? label.style_triangleup : label.style_triangledown)

f_tf() =>
    timeframe.isseconds ? timeframe.period + "s" : timeframe.isminutes ? timeframe.period + "m" : timeframe.period

f_r(float v) =>
    (v >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(v, "#.##")

f_col(int n) =>
    n == 1 ? cN1 : n == 2 ? cN2 : n == 3 ? cN3 : cNx

f_brkDn(float lvl) =>
    na(lvl) ? false : confMode == "Wick beyond" ? low < lvl : confMode == "Close beyond" ? close < lvl : close < lvl and open < lvl

f_brkUp(float lvl) =>
    na(lvl) ? false : confMode == "Wick beyond" ? high > lvl : confMode == "Close beyond" ? close > lvl : close > lvl and open > lvl

// A level can stand longer than TradingView allows a drawing coordinate to sit
// behind the current bar (~10,000). Only the DRAWING is clamped.
f_xc(int x) =>
    na(x) ? bar_index : math.max(x, bar_index - 4000)

// Hard ceiling on drawings, not a setting. TradingView itself cannot draw more
// than 500 lines or labels, so there is no useful choice here.
int keepN = 500

atr14 = ta.atr(14)

// ---- the dead hours --------------------------------------------------------
// One reading per bar, taken from the bar's OPEN time in the chosen zone, so the
// 21:00 candle is the first one inside and the 01:30 candle is the first one out.
// TradingView resolves the zone's daylight saving per date, which is why a
// New York window does not drift by an hour twice a year.
tzUse = thTz == "Exchange" ? syminfo.timezone : thTz
daysUse = thDays == "" ? "1234567" : thDays
// TradingView's own session picker can write a ":days" suffix into the window box.
// Appending a second one would make the session string invalid, so the suffix that is
// already there wins and the days input is only used when there is none.
winUse = str.contains(thWin, ":") ? thWin : thWin + ":" + daysUse
inBlk = thOn and not na(time(timeframe.period, winUse, tzUse))
// "Everything in the window" also silences the drawing and the alerts, not just
// the entry. "Only the entry" leaves the marks on the chart to be looked at.
blkHush = inBlk and thWhat == "Everything in the window"
bgcolor(thShade and inBlk ? thShadeC : na, title = "Dead hours")

// ===================== THE STRUCTURE =========================================
// One entry per SWING, alternating high · low · high · low. swU marks a swing
// price has already broken — a level leaves for that reason and no other.
var array<float> swP = array.new<float>()
var array<int> swB = array.new<int>()
var array<bool> swH = array.new<bool>()
var array<int> swK = array.new<int>()
var array<bool> swU = array.new<bool>()

var int nHL = 0
var int nLH = 0
// Bar of the last swing numbered in the running sequence. A sequence eats
// structure newest-first, so each one must be OLDER than the last. The moment a
// break takes one NEWER than that, the move has started on structure it built
// itself — a different leg — and the count restarts at 1st.
var int lastBhl = -1
var int lastBlh = -1
// Judged once, at the 1st Break, and it holds for the whole sequence. A
// sequence that does not qualify still eats its levels — they were broken, and
// pretending otherwise would leave them standing forever — it just is not drawn,
// entered, or counted. A sequence born inside the dead hours is disqualified the
// same way, and stays disqualified after the window has passed: it is the same
// sequence, and it started in the hours you do not trade.
var bool upQual = true
var bool dnQual = true
var int qSkipUp = 0
var int qSkipDn = 0
// sequences and entries the clock killed — separate from the leg filter, so the
// dashboard shows what each one is actually costing
var int blkSeqUp = 0
var int blkSeqDn = 0
var int blkEnt = 0

var array<line> brkLn = array.new<line>()
var array<label> brkLb = array.new<label>()
var array<line> stkLn = array.new<line>()
var array<label> stkLb = array.new<label>()
var array<label> enLb = array.new<label>()
var array<line> zzLn = array.new<line>()
var array<label> zzLb = array.new<label>()

// ---- results state ---------------------------------------------------------
var int trTot = 0
var int trWin = 0
var int trLoss = 0
var float rSum = 0.0
var float rWin = 0.0
var float rLoss = 0.0
var bool inTrade = false
var bool trLong = false
var float trEntry = na
var float trStop = na
var float trTgt = na
var float trR = na

f_prune(array<line> la, array<label> lb, int k) =>
    while array.size(la) > k
        line.delete(array.shift(la))
    while array.size(lb) > k
        label.delete(array.shift(lb))
    array.size(la)

// Is swing i a level for this side? Every unbroken swing on that side, unless
// the strict reading is on, in which case buys take LH only and sells HL only.
f_isLvl(int i, bool wantHigh) =>
    bool ok = array.get(swH, i) == wantHigh and not array.get(swU, i)
    if ok and lhOnly
        int k = array.get(swK, i)
        ok := wantHigh ? k == 3 : k == 2
    ok

// newest unbroken level on a side, or -1
f_newestLvl(bool wantHigh) =>
    int k = -1
    int n = array.size(swP)
    if n > 0
        for j = 0 to n - 1
            int i = n - 1 - j
            if k == -1 and f_isLvl(i, wantHigh)
                k := i
    k

f_countLvl(bool wantHigh) =>
    int c = 0
    int n = array.size(swP)
    if n > 0
        for i = 0 to n - 1
            if f_isLvl(i, wantHigh)
                c := c + 1
    c

// newest unbroken swing on a side, whatever it is classified as. The structural
// stop sits behind the move, and it sits there whether that swing is an HL or an
// LL — the strict reading filters what gets NUMBERED, not where the idea is wrong.
f_newestSw(bool wantHigh) =>
    int k = -1
    int n = array.size(swP)
    if n > 0
        for j = 0 to n - 1
            int i = n - 1 - j
            if k == -1 and array.get(swH, i) == wantHigh and not array.get(swU, i)
                k := i
    k

// NEAREST unbroken level the other side of `ref` — the next thing in the way
f_nearLvl(bool wantHigh, float ref) =>
    float v = na
    int n = array.size(swP)
    if n > 0
        for i = 0 to n - 1
            if f_isLvl(i, wantHigh)
                float p = array.get(swP, i)
                bool beyond = wantHigh ? p > ref : p < ref
                if beyond
                    v := na(v) ? p : (wantHigh ? math.min(v, p) : math.max(v, p))
    v

// furthest unbroken level on a side — the draw on liquidity
f_farLvl(bool wantHigh) =>
    float v = na
    int n = array.size(swP)
    if n > 0
        for i = 0 to n - 1
            if f_isLvl(i, wantHigh)
                float p = array.get(swP, i)
                v := na(v) ? p : (wantHigh ? math.max(v, p) : math.min(v, p))
    v

// the level this bar takes, newest first, or -1
f_nextUp() =>
    int k = -1
    int n = array.size(swP)
    if n > 0
        for j = 0 to n - 1
            int i = n - 1 - j
            if k == -1 and f_isLvl(i, true) and f_brkUp(array.get(swP, i))
                k := i
    k

f_nextDn() =>
    int k = -1
    int n = array.size(swP)
    if n > 0
        for j = 0 to n - 1
            int i = n - 1 - j
            if k == -1 and f_isLvl(i, false) and f_brkDn(array.get(swP, i))
                k := i
    k

// pivots read unconditionally so their history stays consistent
float rawPl = ta.pivotlow(pvLen, pvLen)
float rawPh = ta.pivothigh(pvLen, pvLen)

// ---- build the alternating structure ---------------------------------------
// A swing high only follows a swing LOW. A higher high arriving while the up leg
// is still running is the SAME swing, moved — not a second level. That is the
// whole difference from reading the two pivot series independently.
// This runs in the dead hours exactly as it does outside them: the window kills
// setups, never the structure they are read from.
bool addedSw = false

if not na(rawPh)
    int b = bar_index - pvLen
    int n = array.size(swP)
    bool sameLeg = false
    if n > 0
        if array.get(swH, n - 1)
            if not array.get(swU, n - 1)
                sameLeg := true
    if sameLeg
        if rawPh > array.get(swP, n - 1)
            array.set(swP, n - 1, rawPh)
            array.set(swB, n - 1, b)
            addedSw := true
    else
        array.push(swP, rawPh)
        array.push(swB, b)
        array.push(swH, true)
        array.push(swK, 0)
        array.push(swU, false)
        addedSw := true

if not na(rawPl)
    int b = bar_index - pvLen
    int n = array.size(swP)
    bool sameLeg = false
    if n > 0
        if not array.get(swH, n - 1)
            if not array.get(swU, n - 1)
                sameLeg := true
    if sameLeg
        if rawPl < array.get(swP, n - 1)
            array.set(swP, n - 1, rawPl)
            array.set(swB, n - 1, b)
            addedSw := true
    else
        array.push(swP, rawPl)
        array.push(swB, b)
        array.push(swH, false)
        array.push(swK, 0)
        array.push(swU, false)
        addedSw := true

// ---- classify the newest swing against the previous one on ITS OWN side -----
if addedSw
    int m = array.size(swP)
    if m > 1
        bool isH = array.get(swH, m - 1)
        float p = array.get(swP, m - 1)
        int prevI = -1
        for j = 0 to m - 2
            int i = m - 2 - j
            if prevI == -1 and array.get(swH, i) == isH
                prevI := i
        int kk = 0
        if prevI >= 0
            float q = array.get(swP, prevI)
            kk := isH ? (p > q ? 1 : 3) : (p > q ? 2 : 4)
        array.set(swK, m - 1, kk)
    while array.size(swP) > swMax
        array.shift(swP)
        array.shift(swB)
        array.shift(swH)
        array.shift(swK)
        array.shift(swU)

// A sequence that ate everything on its side is finished. Checked at the START
// of the bar, so the bar that empties it keeps its own numbering intact.
if f_countLvl(false) == 0
    nHL := 0
if f_countLvl(true) == 0
    nLH := 0

bool evalOk = not waitClose or barstate.isconfirmed
bool sellReady = f_countLvl(false) >= minLv
bool buyReady = f_countLvl(true) >= minLv
bool firedAny = false
int lastNo = 0
float lastLvl = na
bool lastWasHL = false
bool entBuy = false
bool entSell = false

f_mark(int n, float p, int b, int k, bool isHL) =>
    if not hidePast or n <= hidePastN
        color c = f_col(n)
        int xStart = f_xc(b)
        if lineOn
            array.push(brkLn, line.new(xStart, p, bar_index, p, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = c, style = f_lstyle(lineStyleIn), width = lineW))
        if lblOn
            float off = atr14 * lblOff
            float yL = isHL ? p - off : p + off
            int xL = lblPos == "Left" ? xStart : lblPos == "Right" ? bar_index : int(math.avg(xStart, bar_index))
            array.push(brkLb, label.new(xL, yL, f_txt(n, p, k), xloc = xloc.bar_index, yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_none, textcolor = c, size = f_size(lblSzIn)))
        f_prune(brkLn, brkLb, keepN)
    array.size(brkLn)

// A marker on the candle you enter, plus its own text. Two separate labels so
// the text is plain coloured type rather than a chunky filled box. The signal is
// made when the BREAK candle closes; both sit `entShift` candles later, which is
// the candle you actually take.
f_entry(bool isBuy) =>
    float pad = atr14 * entPad
    color c = isBuy ? entBuyC : entSellC
    int x = bar_index + entShift
    array.push(enLb, label.new(x, isBuy ? low - pad : high + pad, "", xloc = xloc.bar_index, yloc = yloc.price, style = f_eshape(entShape, isBuy), color = c, textcolor = c, size = f_size(entSzIn)))
    array.push(enLb, label.new(x, isBuy ? low - pad * 2.4 : high + pad * 2.4, isBuy ? entTxtBuy : entTxtSell, xloc = xloc.bar_index, yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_none, textcolor = c, size = f_size(entTxtSz)))
    while array.size(enLb) > keepN * 2
        label.delete(array.shift(enLb))
    array.size(enLb)

// ---- the move takes the structure back, newest first -----------------------
if evalOk and sellOn and sellReady
    int gi = f_nextDn()
    while gi >= 0
        float p = array.get(swP, gi)
        int b = array.get(swB, gi)
        int k = array.get(swK, gi)
        array.set(swU, gi, true)
        if nHL > 0 and b >= lastBhl
            nHL := 0
        nHL := nHL + 1
        lastBhl := b
        // the 1st Break is where the sequence is judged
        if nHL == 1
            bool okLeg = not qOn
            if qOn
                int hi = f_newestSw(true)
                if hi >= 0
                    okLeg := (array.get(swP, hi) - p) >= minLegAtr * atr14
                    if okLeg and qTrend
                        okLeg := array.get(swK, hi) == 3
            // the clock is judged here too, so a sequence born in the dead hours
            // stays dead for its whole life instead of waking up at 01:30
            bool okHrs = not blkHush
            if okLeg and not okHrs
                blkSeqDn := blkSeqDn + 1
            dnQual := okLeg and okHrs
            if not okLeg
                qSkipDn := qSkipDn + 1
        if dnQual and not blkHush
            firedAny := true
            lastNo := nHL
            lastLvl := p
            lastWasHL := true
        if (dnQual or drawSkipped) and not blkHush
            f_mark(nHL, p, b, k, true)
        if nHL == entAt and dnQual
            if inBlk
                blkEnt := blkEnt + 1
            else
                entSell := true
                if entOn
                    f_entry(false)
        gi := f_nextDn()

if evalOk and buyOn and buyReady
    int gj = f_nextUp()
    while gj >= 0
        float p = array.get(swP, gj)
        int b = array.get(swB, gj)
        int k = array.get(swK, gj)
        array.set(swU, gj, true)
        if nLH > 0 and b >= lastBlh
            nLH := 0
        nLH := nLH + 1
        lastBlh := b
        // the 1st Break is where the sequence is judged
        if nLH == 1
            bool okLeg = not qOn
            if qOn
                int li = f_newestSw(false)
                if li >= 0
                    okLeg := (p - array.get(swP, li)) >= minLegAtr * atr14
                    if okLeg and qTrend
                        okLeg := array.get(swK, li) == 2
            bool okHrs = not blkHush
            if okLeg and not okHrs
                blkSeqUp := blkSeqUp + 1
            upQual := okLeg and okHrs
            if not okLeg
                qSkipUp := qSkipUp + 1
        if upQual and not blkHush
            firedAny := true
            lastNo := nLH
            lastLvl := p
            lastWasHL := false
        if (upQual or drawSkipped) and not blkHush
            f_mark(nLH, p, b, k, false)
        if nLH == entAt and upQual
            if inBlk
                blkEnt := blkEnt + 1
            else
                entBuy := true
                if entOn
                    f_entry(true)
        gj := f_nextUp()

// ===================== RESULTS TRACKER =======================================
// Resolve the OPEN trade first, so the entry bar itself is never used to close
// the trade it just opened. One position at a time; a signal that arrives while
// a trade is open is ignored rather than stacked.
//
// A trade already running when the dead hours start is left alone to hit its
// stop or its target — the window stops setups being TAKEN, it does not
// liquidate one that was.
if resOn and evalOk
    if inTrade
        bool hitStop = trLong ? low <= trStop : high >= trStop
        bool hitTgt = trLong ? high >= trTgt : low <= trTgt
        if hitStop
            trTot := trTot + 1
            trLoss := trLoss + 1
            rSum := rSum - 1.0
            rLoss := rLoss + 1.0
            inTrade := false
        else if hitTgt
            trTot := trTot + 1
            trWin := trWin + 1
            rSum := rSum + trR
            rWin := rWin + trR
            inTrade := false

    if not inTrade and (entBuy or entSell)
        bool isLong = entBuy
        float e = close
        int si = f_newestSw(not isLong)
        float structSt = si >= 0 ? array.get(swP, si) : na
        float st = stopMode == "Fixed × ATR" or na(structSt) ? (isLong ? e - atr14 * stopAtr : e + atr14 * stopAtr) : structSt
        // a stop on the wrong side of entry is no stop at all
        if isLong and st >= e
            st := e - atr14 * stopAtr
        if not isLong and st <= e
            st := e + atr14 * stopAtr
        float risk = math.abs(e - st)
        float tg = na
        if tgtMode == "Nearest opposite level"
            tg := f_nearLvl(isLong, e)
        if tgtMode == "Opposite extreme (draw on liquidity)"
            tg := f_farLvl(isLong)
        if na(tg) or (isLong and tg <= e) or (not isLong and tg >= e)
            tg := isLong ? e + risk * tgtR : e - risk * tgtR
        if risk > 0
            inTrade := true
            trLong := isLong
            trEntry := e
            trStop := st
            trTgt := tg
            trR := math.abs(tg - e) / risk

// ---- keep the chart to the price action being looked at --------------------
if barstate.islast and histBars > 0
    while array.size(brkLn) > 0 and line.get_x2(array.get(brkLn, 0)) < bar_index - histBars
        line.delete(array.shift(brkLn))
    while array.size(brkLb) > 0 and label.get_x(array.get(brkLb, 0)) < bar_index - histBars
        label.delete(array.shift(brkLb))
    while array.size(enLb) > 0 and label.get_x(array.get(enLb, 0)) < bar_index - histBars
        label.delete(array.shift(enLb))

// ===================== STRUCTURE + WHAT IS STILL STANDING ====================
// Both redrawn on the last bar only, so nothing accumulates.
if barstate.islast
    while array.size(stkLn) > 0
        line.delete(array.shift(stkLn))
    while array.size(stkLb) > 0
        label.delete(array.shift(stkLb))
    while array.size(zzLn) > 0
        line.delete(array.shift(zzLn))
    while array.size(zzLb) > 0
        label.delete(array.shift(zzLb))

    int n = array.size(swP)
    if (zzLbl or zzLine) and n > 0
        int from = math.max(0, n - zzN)
        for i = from to n - 1
            float p = array.get(swP, i)
            int b = array.get(swB, i)
            int k = array.get(swK, i)
            bool isH = array.get(swH, i)
            color c = k == 1 or k == 2 ? zzUpC : k == 3 or k == 4 ? zzDnC : color.new(color.gray, 20)
            if zzLine and i > from
                array.push(zzLn, line.new(f_xc(array.get(swB, i - 1)), array.get(swP, i - 1), f_xc(b), p, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = zzLnC, width = 1))
            if zzLbl
                float off = atr14 * 0.3
                array.push(zzLb, label.new(f_xc(b), isH ? p + off : p - off, f_kind(k), xloc = xloc.bar_index, yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_none, textcolor = c, size = size.tiny))

    if stackShow and n > 0
        int rankHi = 0
        int rankLo = 0
        for j = 0 to n - 1
            int i = n - 1 - j
            float p = array.get(swP, i)
            bool isH = array.get(swH, i)
            if (isH and buyOn and f_isLvl(i, true)) or (not isH and sellOn and f_isLvl(i, false))
                int rank = isH ? rankHi + 1 : rankLo + 1
                if isH
                    rankHi := rank
                else
                    rankLo := rank
                color c = isH ? stackLHC : stackHLC
                array.push(stkLn, line.new(f_xc(array.get(swB, i)), p, bar_index + 4, p, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = c, style = line.style_dotted, width = 1))
                if stackTag
                    array.push(stkLb, label.new(bar_index + 5, p, str.tostring(rank), xloc = xloc.bar_index, yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_none, textcolor = c, size = size.tiny))

// ===================== ALERTS ================================================
// An entry alert can never come from inside the dead hours: entBuy and entSell are
// held false there in BOTH modes. The break alert follows the mode — silent inside the
// window on "Everything in the window", still firing on "Only the entry", which is the
// point of that mode: you are watching the hours, not trading them.
alertcondition(firedAny, "Any break", "Basic Breaks — a level was broken")
alertcondition(entBuy, "BUY entry", "Basic Breaks — BUY: the break candle has closed, enter on the next candle")
alertcondition(entSell, "SELL entry", "Basic Breaks — SELL: the break candle has closed, enter on the next candle")
if firedAny
    alert(f_ord(lastNo) + " Break — " + (lastWasHL ? "low" : "high") + " @ " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(lastLvl)), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if entBuy or entSell
    alert((entBuy ? "BUY" : "SELL") + " — " + f_ord(entAt) + " break has closed, enter on the next candle", alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// ===================== DASHBOARD =============================================
var table db = table.new(f_tpos(dbPos), 3, 14, border_width = 1)
f_cell(int col, int row, string txt, color c) =>
    table.cell(db, col, row, txt, text_color = c, text_size = f_size(dbSzIn), bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 85))

if dbOn and barstate.islast
    table.clear(db, 0, 0, 2, 13)
    color gry = color.new(color.gray, 0)

    // the current structure read: the newest swing on each side, whatever it is
    int iH = -1
    int iL = -1
    int n = array.size(swP)
    if n > 0
        for j = 0 to n - 1
            int i = n - 1 - j
            if iH == -1 and array.get(swH, i)
                iH := i
            if iL == -1 and not array.get(swH, i)
                iL := i

    f_cell(0, 0, "BREAKS  " + f_tf(), color.new(color.white, 0))
    f_cell(1, 0, "standing", gry)
    f_cell(2, 0, "broken", gry)
    f_cell(0, 1, "lows  (sells)", color.new(stackHLC, 0))
    f_cell(1, 1, sellOn ? str.tostring(f_countLvl(false)) + (sellReady ? "" : "!") : "—", color.new(stackHLC, sellOn ? 0 : 60))
    f_cell(2, 1, sellOn and nHL > 0 ? f_ord(nHL) : "·", f_col(nHL == 0 ? 4 : nHL))
    f_cell(0, 2, "highs  (buys)", color.new(stackLHC, 0))
    f_cell(1, 2, buyOn ? str.tostring(f_countLvl(true)) + (buyReady ? "" : "!") : "—", color.new(stackLHC, buyOn ? 0 : 60))
    f_cell(2, 2, buyOn and nLH > 0 ? f_ord(nLH) : "·", f_col(nLH == 0 ? 4 : nLH))
    string txtH = "—"
    string txtL = "—"
    color colH = gry
    color colL = gry
    if iH >= 0
        int kH = array.get(swK, iH)
        txtH := f_kind(kH) + "  " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(array.get(swP, iH)))
        colH := kH == 1 ? zzUpC : kH == 3 ? zzDnC : gry
    if iL >= 0
        int kL = array.get(swK, iL)
        txtL := f_kind(kL) + "  " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(array.get(swP, iL)))
        colL := kL == 2 ? zzUpC : kL == 4 ? zzDnC : gry
    f_cell(0, 3, "structure  " + (lhOnly ? "(LH / HL only)" : "(all swings)"), color.new(color.white, 0))
    f_cell(1, 3, txtH, colH)
    f_cell(2, 3, txtL, colL)
    f_cell(0, 4, qOn ? "sequences skipped  (leg < " + str.tostring(minLegAtr, "#.#") + "× ATR)" : "sequences skipped  (filter off)", gry)
    f_cell(1, 4, str.tostring(qSkipUp) + " buy", gry)
    f_cell(2, 4, str.tostring(qSkipDn) + " sell", gry)
    f_cell(0, 5, thOn ? "dead hours  " + thWin + "  " + (thTz == "Exchange" ? "chart tz" : thTz) : "dead hours  (off)", thOn and inBlk ? entSellC : gry)
    f_cell(1, 5, thOn ? str.tostring(blkSeqUp + blkSeqDn) + " seq · " + str.tostring(blkEnt) + " entries" : "—", gry)
    f_cell(2, 5, thOn ? (inBlk ? "IN — nothing fires" : "outside") : "—", thOn ? (inBlk ? entSellC : entBuyC) : gry)

    if resOn
        float wr = trTot > 0 ? 100.0 * trWin / trTot : na
        float avgR = trTot > 0 ? rSum / trTot : na
        float pf = rLoss > 0 ? rWin / rLoss : na
        color pnlC = rSum > 0 ? entBuyC : rSum < 0 ? entSellC : gry
        f_cell(0, 6, f_ord(entAt) + "-break results  ·  " + f_tf(), color.new(color.white, 0))
        f_cell(1, 6, "", gry)
        f_cell(2, 6, "", gry)
        f_cell(0, 7, "trades", gry)
        f_cell(1, 7, str.tostring(trTot), color.new(color.white, 0))
        f_cell(2, 7, inTrade ? (trLong ? "1 open L" : "1 open S") : "", inTrade ? (trLong ? entBuyC : entSellC) : gry)
        f_cell(0, 8, "wins", gry)
        f_cell(1, 8, str.tostring(trWin), entBuyC)
        f_cell(2, 8, na(wr) ? "—" : str.tostring(wr, "#.#") + "%", entBuyC)
        f_cell(0, 9, "losses", gry)
        f_cell(1, 9, str.tostring(trLoss), entSellC)
        f_cell(2, 9, na(wr) ? "—" : str.tostring(100.0 - wr, "#.#") + "%", entSellC)
        f_cell(0, 10, "avg R / trade", gry)
        f_cell(1, 10, na(avgR) ? "—" : f_r(avgR), na(avgR) ? gry : avgR >= 0 ? entBuyC : entSellC)
        f_cell(2, 10, "", gry)
        f_cell(0, 11, "total R", gry)
        f_cell(1, 11, f_r(rSum), pnlC)
        f_cell(2, 11, "", gry)
        f_cell(0, 12, "profit factor", gry)
        f_cell(1, 12, na(pf) ? "—" : str.tostring(pf, "#.##"), na(pf) ? gry : pf >= 1 ? entBuyC : entSellC)
        f_cell(2, 12, "", gry)
        f_cell(0, 13, "R:R on the open trade", gry)
        f_cell(1, 13, inTrade and not na(trR) ? "1 : " + str.tostring(trR, "#.##") : "—", inTrade ? (trLong ? entBuyC : entSellC) : gry)
        f_cell(2, 13, inTrade ? str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(trStop)) + " → " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(trTgt)) : "", gry)
